<Layout title="Radon Testing in Nashville & Middle Tennessee" description="Understand your home’s radon level with Dream Solutions Tennessee. Learn about radon testing, health risks, and the EPA action level."><Hero eyebrow="01 / Radon testing" title="Good decisions start<br />with <em>clear answers.</em>" description="Radon has no color or smell. A test gives you the information you need to make an informed decision about your home." /><section class="split-section"><h2>An invisible gas.<br /><em>A measurable risk.</em></h2><div class="prose"><p>Radon forms naturally as uranium breaks down in soil and rock. It can move through foundation cracks, joints, and other openings and accumulate indoors. Any home can have elevated radon, regardless of age or construction.</p><p>Breathing radon over time increases the risk of lung cancer. Testing is the only way to know the level in your home; a neighbor’s result cannot tell you yours. <a href="https://www.cdc.gov/radon/about/">Learn more from the CDC.</a></p></div></section><section class="process-section"><p class="eyebrow">What to expect</p><h2>A clear path forward.</h2><div class="process-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">01</span><h3>Plan the test</h3><p>We discuss your home, the space to test, and the conditions needed for a useful measurement.</p></div><div><span class="eyebrow">02</span><h3>Measure your air</h3><p>Testing equipment measures radon over the test period. Follow the instructions provided, including any closed-house requirements.</p></div><div><span class="eyebrow">03</span><h3>Understand the result</h3><p>Review the reading and next steps. If mitigation is needed, we can discuss a system suited to your home.</p></div></div></section><aside class="guidance"><p class="eyebrow">Know the number</p><h2>4.0 <small>pCi/L</small></h2><p>The EPA recommends fixing homes with radon levels at or above 4.0 pCi/L and considering action between 2 and 4 pCi/L. There is no known safe level of radon exposure.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.epa.gov/radon/what-epas-action-level-radon-and-what-does-it-mean">Read the EPA’s guidance ↗</a></aside><CallToAction /></Layout>